{# Owner decision D-245 P3: associate commission settings. When commission is paid, the counting-order
   threshold, buyer registration and GST are the MD's (manage_pricing); TDS and the bank waiting days as
   before. Levels and the ladder: Admin → Pricing. PHP twin: views/associates/ladder.php.
   Expects: tdsValue, wait, commission (settings), thresholdValue, gstValue, canPricing, csrfToken. #}
{% set __dis = '' if canPricing else ' disabled' %}
<div class="card">
  <h1>Associates — commission settings</h1>
  <p class="muted">Commission is worked out on the final invoiced FOB of the goods, line by line, at the commission level fixed on each order when its Proforma Invoice is issued, and only once the buyer has paid the order in full. The levels and the ladder are set in <a href="/pricing/commission-levels">Admin &rarr; Pricing &rarr; Commission levels</a>.</p>
  <form method="post" action="/associates/ladder">
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
    <fieldset><legend>When commission is paid {% if not canPricing %}<small class="muted">(the MD changes these)</small>{% endif %}</legend>
      <div class="field-grid">
        <label>Days after full payment *<input type="number" name="associate_commission_due_days" required min="0" max="365" step="1" value="{{ commission.due_days }}" placeholder="e.g. 30"{{ __dis }}><span class="help-line">Example: 30 → buyer pays in full on 4 Nov, commission due on 4 Dec.</span></label>
        <label>Payout run *<select name="associate_payout_run" required{{ __dis }}><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="monthly"{{ ' selected' if commission.run == 'monthly' }}>Monthly</option><option value="weekly"{{ ' selected' if commission.run == 'weekly' }}>Weekly</option></select><span class="help-line">Example: monthly → commission due on 4 Dec is paid in the run on 5 Jan (the first run on or after the due date).</span></label>
        <label>Payout day * <small class="muted">(1–28 for monthly; 1 = Monday … 7 = Sunday for weekly)</small><input type="number" name="associate_payout_day" required min="1" max="28" step="1" value="{{ commission.day }}" placeholder="e.g. 5"{{ __dis }}><span class="help-line">Example: 5 → runs on the 5th of every month.</span></label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" name="associate_claim_hold" value="1"{{ ' checked' if commission.claim_hold }}{{ __dis }}> Hold while a buyer claim (raised on or before the due date) is open</label>
        <label>Commission period shown to associates *<select name="associate_portal_commission_months" required{{ __dis }}><option value="">Choose…</option>{% for __m in [3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18, 24] %}<option value="{{ __m }}"{{ ' selected' if commission.portal_months == __m }}>{{ __m }} months</option>{% endfor %}</select><span class="help-line">Example: 12 → in the portal an associate sees only the commission of the last 12 months (totals and list); commission still waiting to be paid is always shown. Staff screens show everything.</span></label>
      </div>
      <div class="field-grid">
        <label>Bank charges of a transfer abroad *<select name="associate_abroad_charges" required{{ __dis }}><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="OUR"{{ ' selected' if commission.abroad_charges == 'OUR' }}>OUR — NexaCrest pays its own and the intermediary bank's charges (the associate receives the full amount)</option><option value="SHA"{{ ' selected' if commission.abroad_charges == 'SHA' }}>SHA — NexaCrest pays its own bank's charges; the associate's bank may charge on receipt</option></select><span class="help-line">D-264: bank charges are never deducted from commission. In India NexaCrest pays the (small) charges.</span></label>
        <label>Minimum payout abroad (USD) *<input type="number" name="associate_abroad_min_payout_usd" required min="0" max="100000" step="0.01" value="{{ commission.abroad_min_usd | fixed2 }}" placeholder="e.g. 100.00"{{ __dis }}><span class="help-line">Example: 100 → an associate abroad with only USD 60 due in a run is paid in the next run, so one transfer's charges are not spent on a small amount.</span></label>
      </div>
      <p class="small muted">After payment a commission is never taken back, except for the associate's fraud or breach of the agreement — with a written reason.</p>
    </fieldset>
    <fieldset><legend>Ladder and registration {% if not canPricing %}<small class="muted">(the MD changes these)</small>{% endif %}</legend>
      <div class="field-grid">
        <label>Counting order: invoiced FOB at least (₹) *<input type="number" name="associate_counting_threshold_inr" required min="0" step="1" value="{{ thresholdValue }}" placeholder="e.g. 500000"{{ __dis }}><span class="help-line">Example: ₹5,00,000 → an order of ₹6 lakh counts toward the next ladder step; one of ₹2 lakh earns the current rate but does not count.</span></label>
        <label>Buyer registration valid (months) *<input type="number" name="associate_protection_months" required min="1" max="60" step="1" value="{{ commission.registration_months }}" placeholder="e.g. 6"{{ __dis }}><span class="help-line">Example: 6 → a buyer registered on 1 Jan who has not ordered by 1 Jul is no longer linked to the associate.</span></label>
        <label>GST on commission (%) * <small class="muted">(GST-registered associates, once their tax invoice is on file)</small><input type="number" name="associate_gst_pct" required min="0" max="28" step="0.01" value="{{ gstValue }}" placeholder="e.g. 18.00"{{ __dis }}><span class="help-line">Example: 18 → commission ₹10,000 + GST ₹1,800 when the associate is GST-registered and their tax invoice is on file.</span></label>
        <label>Zoho GST tax for commission <small class="muted">(the Zoho Books tax id booked on the associate's bill when GST is paid on top; empty = the sync refuses such a bill)</small><input type="text" name="zoho_gst_commission_tax_id" maxlength="40" pattern="[0-9A-Za-z_\-]*" value="{{ commission.zoho_gst_tax_id }}" placeholder="e.g. 460000000012345"{{ __dis }}><span class="help-line">Example: an associate's tax invoice of ₹10,000 + GST ₹1,800 → the Zoho bill shows ₹11,800 with this GST tax, so the bill matches the payment and the ₹1,800 input credit is booked.</span></label>
      </div>
    </fieldset>
    <div class="field-grid">
      <label>TDS on commission, India (section 194H) % *<input type="number" name="associate_tds_pct" required min="0" max="30" step="0.01" value="{{ tdsValue }}" placeholder="e.g. 2.00"></label> <small class="muted">Threshold, rate without PAN and the rules for associates abroad: <a href="/settings/associate-tds">Settings &rarr; Associate TDS</a>.</small>
      <label>Wait before a new bank account is used (days) *<input type="number" name="associate_bank_wait_days" required min="0" max="60" step="1" value="{{ wait }}" placeholder="e.g. 7"></label>
    </div>
    <div class="btn-row"><button type="submit">Save</button> <a href="/associates">Back to associates</a></div>
  </form>
</div>
